// x-rerun-1-01: graphix-fuzz wraps the body as `let result = {<body>` with no
// newline, so a body whose first line is a comment (every `// expect: reject`
// pin, every finding file's header) is a parse error at line 1 of /test.
//
// command: graphix-fuzz check design/review-2026-10-12/repro/x-rerun-1-01.gx
//
// expected: DIVERGENCE or a failure: this program is valid (it yields 2), so
// a pin claiming `expect: reject` over it should not agree.
// observed: AGREE (reject); `graphix-fuzz run` shows CompileErr "a comment
// stands on a line of its own" at `use super::*; let result = {// ...`.
// The fuzzer keeps only its own header line below; strip_header drops the
// others, so the program the fuzzer sees starts with it.
// expect: reject
let x = 1;
x + 1
